# Structural Telework Annex to the Employment Contract (CCT n° 85)

**Employee:** Pieter De Smet (E1063), Senior Software Engineer, Engineering (Brussels)

1. **Place of telework:** the employee's home address, Rue Vanderkindere 212, 1180 Uccle, Belgium. **Any change of the place of telework requires a written amendment of this annex.**
2. **Frequency:** 3 days per week (Monday, Wednesday, Friday). Tuesday and Thursday at the Brussels office.
3. **Working time and availability:** 38 hours per week according to the work regulations; reachable during core hours 9:30–12:00 and 14:00–16:00.
4. **Equipment:** laptop, screen, headset provided by the employer; home-office allowance according to the Home Office Allowance Policy.
5. **Data protection:** VPN mandatory; no storage of company data on private devices.
6. **Accidents:** accidents during telework at the place of telework are presumed to be work accidents under the legal conditions.
7. **Termination of telework:** either party may end structural telework with one month's notice; the employee then returns to the office full-time.
8. **Reference:** CCT n° 85 of 9 November 2005 on telework.

Brussels, 18 March 2024. For the employer: Elke Wouters (Engineering Manager), Catherine Lemaire (HR Director). Employee: Pieter De Smet.

